{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641942,"nonce":"Njxgr9cN1H/pVZ+L5nISxqNhKqA=","title":"Large pool blocks take the global registry mutex on alloc, free and realloc","message":"collector.rs note_large, forget_large and large_total take the global REGISTRY mutex and operate on a BTreeMap for every pool allocation, free and realloc above 2048 bytes. zyntax_free takes the same lock for every non-slab pointer, including foreign ones, before passing it to libc. A large realloc does three locked map operations plus alloc, copy and free instead of libc realloc.\n\nRepro: list(range(300)) (2,400 bytes) in a loop costs about 1.2 us in zypy vs 0.77 us for list(range(250)), which stays pooled; about 0.3 us per block is registry plus libc round trip. With ZYNTAX_PARALLEL_LOOPS every large allocation serialises on the one mutex. Dict index arrays above 256 slots and Lua arrays above 256 elements take this path.\n\nDirection: per-slab or sharded table, or a header that carries the length.","files":null}]}